\section{Coercion-Based Compilation}\label{sec:coercion-compilation}

In coercion-based compilation, subtyping is implemented by inserting explicit coercion functions that convert values from one representation to another.

\subsection{Coercions for Subtyping}\label{sec:coercions-subtyping}

\begin{example}[Numeric coercions]\label{ex:numeric-coercions}
If $\mathrm{int} <: \mathrm{float}$, the expression $3.14 + 42$ is compiled as:
\[
  3.14 + \mathrm{coerce}_{\mathrm{int} \to \mathrm{float}}(42)
\]
The coercion function converts the integer 42 to the floating-point value 42.0.
\end{example}

\subsection{Coercions for Records}\label{sec:coercions-records}

For width subtyping, the coercion projects the required fields:

\begin{verbatim}
  -- Source:
  let dog : Dog = { name = "Rex", breed = "Lab", age = 3 }
  let animal : Animal = dog  -- width subtyping

  -- Compiled:
  let animal : Animal = coerce_Dog_to_Animal(dog)
  -- coerce_Dog_to_Animal projects the name and age fields
\end{verbatim}

